      <h1>How Bitcoin Reaches Consensus</h1>
      <p class="msc-learn-page__deck">Bitcoin consensus is the shared set of validation rules that independently operated nodes use to decide which transactions and blocks are valid. Proof of work orders valid competing chain history, but it does not replace validation. Bitcoin reaches practical agreement because nodes apply compatible rules to the same public data, reject rule-breaking blocks, and select the valid candidate chain with the greatest accumulated work.</p>
      <ul class="msc-learn-page-meta"><li>Consensus</li><li>Deep</li><li>Technical Analysis</li><li>15 minutes</li><li>Reviewed 2026-07-19</li></ul>
